r, computer). Weakness: communication (nasty remarks) and memory for numbers (attention). Could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Negatives: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Weakness: communication, teamwork, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Negatives: regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Weakness: crew cooperation (know-it-all, hot temper) may affect teamwork.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some weaknesses. Which candidate has strongest overall? Let's weigh criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: reliability high, stress resilience high, technical competence moderate (weather, computer), decision quality not mentioned, attention weak (memory for numbers), communication poor (nasty remarks). So crew cooperation low.\n\nCandidate C: decision quality high, stress resilience high, technical competence high, but communication poor, egocentric, not willing to learn (adaptability low). Crew cooperation low.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility high, attention high, problem solving high, adaptability moderate (responds to unexpected), but crew cooperation low (know-it-all, hot temper). No explicit stress resilience, but responds to unexpected events adequately maybe indicates some. No explicit reliability.\n\nCandidate A: anticipation (decision quality), technical competence (complex connections, spatial vision), leadership (crew cooperation), but not open to new ideas (adaptability low), show-off (communication). Reliability not explicit but leadership suggests.\n\nWhich candidate has least severe weaknesses? B's nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. C's egocentric and communication difficulty also serious. D's hot temper also serious. A's show-off and not open to new ideas also problematic but maybe less severe? Show-off could affect crew morale, not open to new ideas affects adaptability. But A has strong leadership and anticipation.\n\nThus maybe A is best overall despite some concerns. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate A, but we need to justify with facts.\n\nWe can say: Based on anticipation of dangerous situations (decision quality), ability to see complex connections (technical competence), excellent spatial vision (operational skill), and very good leadership (crew cooperation), A stands out. The concerns (show-off, not open to new ideas) are noted but may be mitigated with training, and they are less critical than the communication issues of B, C, D.\n\nThus vote for Candidate A.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\"."}
